lliquid assets and total assets. These empirical results provide evidence to support the hypothesis about the positive relationship between PFA and saving behaviors. I also find that the self-control ability has a significant positive relationship with annual total savings, emergency funds, financial assets and total assets. These empirical results support the hypothesis about the positive relationship between self-control ability and saving behaviors. The interaction term of PFA and self-control has a significant negative relationship with financial assets and total loans, at the 0.1 significance level. These findings support the hypothesis that people with lower levels of self-control can benefit more by getting professional financial advice than those with higher levels of self-control.},
