  abstract = {The article discusses the cost of consumer credit. Due to consumers' unfamiliarity with credit finance structures, there is a significant amount of confusion and misinformation regarding installment charges. An analysis of finance charges is presented. The critical terms, which determine how charges are calculated are 'constant ratio,' 'actuarial yield,' and 'direct ratio.' A common misconception is that bank charges are lower than finance company charges; they are nearly identical. Both those extending the lines of credit and the consumers using the credit are not adequately informed of their costs.},
